  "foaf:name": "Convex Seascape Survey",
  "sdo:name": "Convex Seascape Survey",
  "sdo:description": "The Convex Seascape Survey is a 5-year, global research project focused on one of the critical un-solved questions of our time: how can healthy oceans help combat climate change? Directly addressing Ocean Decade Challenge 5, the survey is generating knowledge on the ocean-climate nexus, specifically focusing on the little-studied carbon stored in the seascape and sediments over the global continental shelves. This multi-million dollar collaboration between Blue Marine Foundation, the University of Exeter and Convex Group Limited, brings together the expertise and resources needed to deliver new open-source data which will enable informed decisions on ocean use. Working with a consortium of 16 other global partners, academics are investigating: Where, why and how does carbon become buried in the seafloor? Where does it come from? What role does life and biodiversity play? And what are the impacts of human disturbance vs. protection?",
  "sdo:location": "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland (UK)",
  "sdo:identifier": "52.6",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/convex-seascape-survey/",
